      "recallAtK": 1,
      "reciprocalRank": 1,
      "answer": "To stub an API response in a Playwright test, you can use the `page.route` method to intercept and modify the response. Here's an example:\n\n```js\nawait page.route('**/api/fetch_data_third_party_dependency', route => route.fulfill({\n  status: 200,\n  body: testData,\n}));\nawait page.goto('https://example.com');\n```\n\nThe advice suggests avoiding testing third-party dependencies [doc-03#0006]. It recommends not testing external sites or third-party servers that you don't control, as this can slow down your tests and is outside your control. Instead, use the Playwright Network API to guarantee the response needed for your tests.",
