      "recallAtK": 0.5,
      "reciprocalRank": 0.5,
      "answer": "To turn on automatic retries for Playwright tests in CI, you can configure the `retries` option in your Playwright configuration file or pass it as a command-line flag. Here's how you can do it:\n\n### Configuration File\nEdit your `playwright.config.ts` file and set the `retries` option:\n\n```js title=\"playwright.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  retries: 3, // Number of retries for failing tests\n});\n```\n\n### Command Line\nYou can also specify the number of retries directly when running the tests:\n\n```bash\nnpx playwright test --retries=3\n```\n\n### Inspecting Reruns\nWhen a test fails and is retried, Playwright will automatically generate a trace for each retry. You can view these traces using the Playwright Trace Viewer, which provides a detailed timeline and inspection capabilities.\n\n1. **Generate a Trace**: Run your tests with tracing enabled:\n    ```bash\n    npx playwright test --trace on\n    ```\n\n2. **View the Trace**: After the tests run, you can open the trace in the Trace Viewer by running:\n    ```bash\n    npx playwright show-trace <trace-file>.zip\n    ```\n\nBy using the Trace Viewer, you can inspect each retry in detail, view network requests, DOM snapshots, and other information to diagnose flaky tests.",
