      "reciprocalRank": 1,
      "answer": "Your assertion is timing out because it's waiting for a condition to be met within the default 5-second timeout, not the 30-second test timeout. To retry a custom value until it matches, you can use `expect.poll`.\n\n```js\nconst result = await expect.poll(async () => {\n  const value = await page.textContent('some-selector');\n  return value === 'expectedValue';\n}, { timeout: 30000, interval: 1000 });\n```\n\nThis code will keep polling every second for up to 30 seconds, checking if the text content of `some-selector` matches `expectedValue`. If it does, it will return `true`; otherwise, it will continue to retry until the timeout is reached.\n\nFor more details, see the [Assertions guide](./test-assertions.md#polling) [doc-15#0007].",
